{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/614-promethean-and-crossovers","id":614,"title":"Promethean and crossovers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-01T15:58:36-07:00","id":614,"title":"Promethean and crossovers","content":"A brainstorm thread. Which other supernaturals are best for crossing over as player characters in to a Promethean chronicle? Would you make any supernatural immune to the Disquiet? Do you think a Mummy may see a Promethean as a similar (in albeit scant ways) immortal soul in a human form?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T16:13:11-07:00","id":636,"title":"","content":"Mike and I looked at some of this in the Rivers of Death episode of Darker Days. The interesting part is how the Osirans, the rivers of the Underworld, and the Duat all interrelate. More than likely the Disquiet for Mummies would cause an interruption in the command of the Judges over the Arisen. A mummy more than likely sees Created as an imperfect version of the Arisen, since the manner in the creation is similar - but where the Arisen retain their original soul, a Created is creating one using Azoth.<br /> <br /> Demon offers even more questions, as the Quashilim are not Angels, and so the question is if the energy of the Principle comes from a source similar to the Abraxas, and so the Prometheans are a spanner in the works of the God Machine/Demiurge, since they are new souls added to the world, and so a chaos factor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.darker-days.org\" target=\"_blank\">www.darker-days.org</a> - The Premier World of Darkness Podcast<br /> Co-designer and miniature painter for Noble Armada 3e<br /> Staff writer for CYBR Magazine <a href=\"https://shop.cybrmagazine.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://shop.cybrmagazine.com/</a><br /> Writer, developer, editor, layout for Darker Days Radio Publishing<br /> Writer for Cubicle 7 Wrath and Glory Revised","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/128-dr-ether","name":"Dr Ether","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar128_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T02:19:17-07:00","id":1000,"title":"","content":"If you make Mages immune to Disquiet, or allow for liberal applications of the Mind Arcanum as a stop gap for it, Prometheans and Mages have a lot of crossover potential. Qashmals and Exarchs, mad hubris, Pyros/Prime...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T04:40:49-07:00","id":1047,"title":"","content":"I would actually suggest Pyros is not Prime. Aetheric Resonance of Demon is more close to Prime. Pyros is the stuff above it all form the Abraxas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.darker-days.org\" target=\"_blank\">www.darker-days.org</a> - The Premier World of Darkness Podcast<br /> Co-designer and miniature painter for Noble Armada 3e<br /> Staff writer for CYBR Magazine <a href=\"https://shop.cybrmagazine.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://shop.cybrmagazine.com/</a><br /> Writer, developer, editor, layout for Darker Days Radio Publishing<br /> Writer for Cubicle 7 Wrath and Glory Revised","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/128-dr-ether","name":"Dr Ether","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar128_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T04:55:12-07:00","id":1056,"title":"","content":"I also agree that Pyros/Prime is dull. Mages don't need the tools to deal with it built in, they're experts at finding the correct tools to use after all so let them hunt down the tools and use those.<br /> <br /> Anyways their other arcana allow for plenty of interaction. Forces and lightning, Life/Death to interact with their flesh, Matter and alchemy, Fate and destiny linking with their pilgrimage, Space and their Wastelands leaving massive sympathetic links, Mind to investigate Disquiet, etc.<br /> <br /> Promethean's are still made of material components, their internal power source/soul/etc. may be very different but the components they are made of are the same.<br /> <br /> Plus hey, Soul Handling. If you're unpleasant enough to want to you could try and see what an artificial soul is like.<br /> <br /> That could be interesting actually. A Mysterium hideyhole is filled with magic stuff and someone has brought back a Promethean's incomplete soul for study. The rest of the Mage Consilium/Cabal/Whatever haven;t heard from that hideyhole or the Mages therein for several weeks and start investigating. At the same time Promethean(s) are drawn to investigate it too and the groups collide for some mistrustful alliances.<br /> <br /> I would probably allow for Mind magic to soothe (but not cancel out) Disquiet. A Mind shield could reduce the Disquiet dice pool by it's rating or something so it's still there but much more manageable. Use of Prime/Life/Spirit/etc. magic could help to fight back against Wastelands too - neither side should be 100% better than the other but something like rerouting Lay Lines could counteract the Wasteland effect or bringing in powerful enough Spirits to feed essence back into the place could reverse the effects and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T10:12:45-07:00","id":1144,"title":"","content":"If I recall, in one of the Promethean books it says Pyros and Promethean are one of the few things Mage don't really understand. Also, I might have imagined reading this, but Wasteland has an averse affect on Magic. I might just be biased though, Mage rubs me the worng way","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T10:23:35-07:00","id":1147,"title":"","content":"Sure Mages might not know much about Prometheans. But as their entire schtick is finding stuff out and your game is a crossover between them then...Mages should really start learning about them! They can't go down to the Mysterium library and find 'Prometheans 101' or 'Top 10 Prometheans Of All Time!' like they could for Vampires. Instead they're going to be the ones writing the books about Prometheans.<br /> <br /> Wastelands may well negatively affect magic. If you're doing a crossover between them then allow Mages to have ways of counteracting it. My example above was to redirect Lay Lines into the Wasteland to reverse the effect or putting a powerful enough Spirit in there to pump in Essence. Make it a problem but not an insurmountable one (and not one that needs ridiculous amounts of player effort else you end up hijacking the game into a convoluted plot to allow the Mages to use their magic or just segregate the groups).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T14:54:01-07:00","id":1315,"title":"","content":"Hmmmm... I'd say Sin-Eaters could make for some fun crossover for a mixed splat player group. Either you have a Sin-Eater cult with a Promethean exploring the Underworld together. The Osirian lineage would be very apropos as they are the lineage most likely to return from death again and again and again. It might make them seek to understand Mortality by courting Death. Add to that their Wasteland effect, turning water into sludge. What would that do to the Rivers of Death?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">Malkavian Madness Forum</a> - Your pbp fix. Be it nWoD, cWoD, CoC, D&amp;D or something else entirely, come over here and get your game on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/348-infernalgoose","name":"InfernalGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T07:01:09-08:00","id":1726,"title":"","content":"I'm stealing here directly from a &quot;101 Plot Hooks for Promethean&quot;...<br /> Fetches. I'd make them immune to Disquiet, if only for the potential of drama when they become among the only &quot;normal&quot; buddies Prometheans can afford to have... and their Changeling comes back and tries to murder the unaware impostor. (Whether Changelings <i>are</i> affected by Disquiet or not is less important, I think; in that scenario, they'd already have pretty good reasons for hating the soulless simulacra of real people, particularly if they start befriending each other.)<br /> What does it bring? Questions about one's identity. On the worth of a sentient being that lacks a soul through no fault of its own. On the designated role of Prometheans as (sometimes) replacement for actual individuals. On revenge. On misplacing one's rightful rage. On the suffering you cause just by existing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T07:03:14-08:00","id":1731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChairKicker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/614-promethean-and-crossovers?p=1726#post1726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm stealing here directly from a &quot;101 Plot Hooks for Promethean&quot;...<br /> Fetches. I'd make them immune to Disquiet, if only for the potential of drama when they become among the only &quot;normal&quot; buddies Prometheans can afford to have... and their Changeling comes back and tries to murder the unaware impostor. (Whether Changelings <i>are</i> affected by Disquiet or not is less important, I think; in that scenario, they'd already have pretty good reasons for hating the soulless simulacra of real people, particularly if they start befriending each other.)<br /> What does it bring? Questions about one's identity. On the worth of a sentient being that lacks a soul through no fault of its own. On the designated role of Prometheans as (sometimes) replacement for actual individuals. On revenge. On misplacing one's rightful rage. On the suffering you cause just by existing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I gave you a thumbs up, as I can't help but love that idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T07:34:45-08:00","id":1750,"title":"","content":"I don't really deserve credit for this one; I'd go and tell who is to thank for the plot hook, but all the forums the idea could have been posted don't have the search function enabled. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T07:41:27-08:00","id":1754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>InfernalGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/614-promethean-and-crossovers?p=1315#post1315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmmm... I'd say Sin-Eaters could make for some fun crossover for a mixed splat player group. Either you have a Sin-Eater cult with a Promethean exploring the Underworld together. The Osirian lineage would be very apropos as they are the lineage most likely to return from death again and again and again. It might make them seek to understand Mortality by courting Death. Add to that their Wasteland effect, turning water into sludge. What would that do to the Rivers of Death?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;But I turn water to sludge! Won't that affect the River?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, it's made of scorpions anyway, so I can't see it hurting...&quot;<br /> <br /> I reckon a Promethean would cause huge amounts of debate within the Sin-Eater academic community, which would be fun to watch. I would personally say that Sin-Eaters are at least resistant to Disquiet since, hey, who are they to judge about the natural order of the world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T11:53:27-08:00","id":1917,"title":"","content":"I was considering a Sin-Eater chronicle with a pirate motif and the thought of adding a Promethean in it brought one word to my mind...<br /> <br /> &quot;Goonies&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/237-dagcon-faraday","name":"Dagcon Faraday","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T08:39:30-08:00","id":2646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/614-promethean-and-crossovers?p=1754#post1754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;But I turn water to sludge! Won't that affect the River?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, it's made of scorpions anyway, so I can't see it hurting...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Sludge scorpions? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">Malkavian Madness Forum</a> - Your pbp fix. Be it nWoD, cWoD, CoC, D&amp;D or something else entirely, come over here and get your game on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/348-infernalgoose","name":"InfernalGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T10:21:21-08:00","id":2739,"title":"","content":"It would probably piss the Kerberoi the hell off though. If the Promethean comes in and starts to literally destroy the particular section of the Underworld then that's going to break all manner of Old Laws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T12:28:25-08:00","id":2831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/614-promethean-and-crossovers?p=2739#post2739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would probably piss the Kerberoi the hell off though. If the Promethean comes in and starts to literally destroy the particular section of the Underworld then that's going to break all manner of Old Laws.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I love Promethean <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Yeah, leave it to the Created to destroy the very realm of death with their tainted presence. The very land rejects them, even in death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">Malkavian Madness Forum</a> - Your pbp fix. Be it nWoD, cWoD, CoC, D&amp;D or something else entirely, come over here and get your game on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/348-infernalgoose","name":"InfernalGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T15:41:00-08:00","id":2954,"title":"","content":"[Reminder to all discussing Prometheans in the Underworld that the Great Below is more slowly affected by the Wasteland to begin with.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T05:53:34-08:00","id":3401,"title":"","content":"I've long believed that a mage of the Uncrowned Kings Legacy could well make an excellent friend/ally/pen-pal for a Promethean. Similar viewpoints on alchemy as metaphor for the state of the soul, plus the mental/soul shields that the Kings get from their attainments can easily be houseruled as helping to resist the effects of Disquiet to a degree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T08:17:46-08:00","id":7360,"title":"","content":"My Crossover Chronicle has two Vampires, a Mage, a Sin-Eater, and Promethean. No one is flat-out immune to Disquiet, though the Bound's Passion Shroud gives her a bonus to rolls to resist it, and the Mage could learn Mind spells to protect against or counter Disquiet. Pyros and Prime are NOT the same thing, and in fact the crossover guide in Tome of the Mysteries flat-out states that Mages cannot manipulate Pyros. The thing about Prometheans is that they're pretty much on the outs with EVERYONE. No one actually likes having them around, and while the Crossover team appreciates the Promethean's abilities, they are well aware that there are extra complications inherent in bringing him anywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T17:45:06-08:00","id":9345,"title":"","content":"The <i>qashmallim</i> makean appearance in <b>Demon: the Descent</b>! They are <i>not</i> angels of the God-Machine, although some demons theorize that they used to be: the implication is that the Principle co-opted angels from the God-Machine, making them kind of \u201cfallen angels\u201d, but not really. <i>If</i> that theory is true.<br /> <br /> I like the theory; although it has some implications: for instance, there ought to be <i>four</i> kinds of <i>qashmallim</i>, not two: Elpidim correspond roughly to Messengers and Lilithim correspond roughly to Destroyers; but there ought to be counterparts to Guardians and Psychopomps as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-12-2013, 08:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T21:06:11-08:00","id":9449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/614-promethean-and-crossovers?p=9345#post9345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the theory; although it has some implications: for instance, there ought to be <i>four</i> kinds of <i>qashmallim</i>, not two: Elpidim correspond roughly to Messengers and Lilithim correspond roughly to Destroyers; but there ought to be counterparts to Guardians and Psychopomps as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being that the Incarnations are loose groupings and this insistence that there ought to be a strict one-to-one equivalence smacks of symmetry for its own sake? No.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T09:53:18-08:00","id":9782,"title":"","content":"Maybe the Principle just don't have any need of Guardians and Psychopomps, and if you think a bit about it it does make sense. Psychopomps especially, as the Principle doesn't need Infraestructure of any sort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T10:18:29-08:00","id":9800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/614-promethean-and-crossovers?p=9345#post9345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <i>qashmallim</i> makean appearance in <b>Demon: the Descent</b>! They are <i>not</i> angels of the God-Machine, although some demons theorize that they used to be: the implication is that the Principle co-opted angels from the God-Machine, making them kind of \u201cfallen angels\u201d, but not really. <i>If</i> that theory is true.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or vice versa <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In my head-canon all Angels are refined from other supernatural entities, in the same way one religion will incorporate the mythos of another. In this way the God-Machine approaches true Godhood. Similarly a Demon's Cipher is the revelation of what mythos it used to be part of, and thus the 'Hell' it seeks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T11:06:08-08:00","id":9848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/614-promethean-and-crossovers?p=9782#post9782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the Principle just don't have any need of Guardians and Psychopomps, and if you think a bit about it it does make sense. Psychopomps especially, as the Principle doesn't need Infraestructure of any sort.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or the Principle just defines Chiors by intent rather than method. Guarding a terrible dictator, or killing a great builder would both be a job for the Lilithm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T11:33:58-08:00","id":9866,"title":"","content":"Or it has more to do with which flavor of Pyros the angel was repurposed to run off of: just like the Unchained have to adapt to living off of Aether instead of Essence, you could say that the Principle repurposes the angels it co-opts to be fueled by either Elpis or Flux.<br /> <br /> But in favor of the \u201cfour Choirs\u201d side of things, it might be possible to revise the concept of Pyros from a duality-based setup to a Great Work setup: Nigredo-flavored Pyros would be Flux and would fuel the Lilithim (who tear thing down); Rubedo-flavored Pyros would be Elpis and would fuel the Elpidos (who guide Prometheans on their Pilgrimages); Albedo-flavored Pyros would be a third type devoted more toward healing and fortifying than evolving or destroying; and Citrinitas-flavored Pyros would be a fourth type dealing with bringing together things previously separate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T11:54:37-08:00","id":9880,"title":"","content":"Why are we assuming the Unchained are accurate to say that the Principle co-opts angels?<br /> <br /> For one thing, Angels fall but the Principles servants never do. Which one sounds like the co-opted knock off? (Ok, neither really)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T12:20:28-08:00","id":9901,"title":"","content":"Per the \u201cco-opted angels\u201d theory, <i>qashmallim</i> don\u2019t Fall because they\u2019ve <i>already</i> \u201cfallen\u201d \u2014 just not in the same way that the Unchained Fell. <br /> <br /> And we\u2019re not assuming that the Unchained <i>are</i> right about <i>qashmallim</i>; we\u2019re assuming that they <i>might be</i> right. That is, they\u2019re not obviously wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T11:18:50-08:00","id":10587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/614-promethean-and-crossovers?p=9800#post9800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or vice versa <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In my head-canon all Angels are refined from other supernatural entities, in the same way one religion will incorporate the mythos of another. In this way the God-Machine approaches true Godhood. Similarly a Demon's Cipher is the revelation of what mythos it used to be part of, and thus the 'Hell' it seeks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that's kind of cool.<br /> <br /> When I ran my first Promethean chronicle, they crossed paths with vampires, werewolves and mages, and it was all very interesting. Highlights:<br /> <br /> 1) A vampire feeding a Promethean lots of blood, trying to bind her. It didn't work, she just got addicted. <br /> 2) The Promethean on the Refinement of Cobalt hooking up with the Bone Shadow Irraka. Um. <br /> 3) Tremere mage (Mama Desta) removing the &quot;soul&quot; from a Promethean. THE DIVINE FIRE IS NOT A SOUL, DUMBASS. The resulting firestorm was unpleasant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T11:31:25-08:00","id":10598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/614-promethean-and-crossovers?p=10587#post10587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I ran my first Promethean chronicle, they crossed paths with vampires, werewolves and mages, and it was all very interesting. Highlights:<br /> <br /> 1) A vampire feeding a Promethean lots of blood, trying to bind her. It didn't work, she just got addicted.<br /> 2) The Promethean on the Refinement of Cobalt hooking up with the Bone Shadow Irraka. Um.<br /> 3) Tremere mage (Mama Desta) removing the &quot;soul&quot; from a Promethean. THE DIVINE FIRE IS NOT A SOUL, DUMBASS. The resulting firestorm was unpleasant.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my own game, which is heavily crossover, the group Ulgan Lazarus is on a soul search to figure out what sort of being he wants to become. So he's super-inquisitive towards other supernaturals, and has the Transmutations that allow him to masquerade as other types, currently Vampires or Mages. The both of which have gotten him into a right bit of trouble.<br /> <br /> Lazarus has...<ul><li>Been kidnapped by a Ordo Dracul member, who mistook him for a Vampire who'd somehow conquered <b>ALL </b>vampiric banes and attempted to dissect him.</li> <li>Accidentally gotten caught up in a Quintessence harvest of an Archmage, whose magical signatures he was investigating.</li> <li>Been taken into a Mage's organization, which his wasteland has steadily turned into a massive spirit den. Which Mage's mistakenly assumed is an attack against him, causing them to keep him under tighter guard, which only makes things worse.</li> <li>He was almost mistaken for Kindred by a member of VII, who would have done his damnedest to kill Laz had other conflicts not intervened (they are now allies).</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T15:33:30-08:00","id":11628,"title":"","content":"Vampires have the most thematic crossover potential, from either direction. Both are obsessed with their own humanity, both need humans to thrive, and both are resurrected corpses cast out of society by their transformation. If ever I did run a Promethean-Kindred crossover, I'd put rebirth back on the table for the vamps. It'd throw a wrench in the Requiem, for sure, and also put the Pilgrimage into question as well.<br /> <br /> I'm not so keen on crossing over with the other splats, as they tend to deal with cosmology over character. Werewolves are too alien, mages too powerful and existentially confusing, changelings offer a bizarre sympathy.... I can see sin-eaters working alright, since their domain is pretty much core, and Promethean bodies carry a lot of baggage thanatologically speaking. Demons and Mummies seem too far out there, though Cover reacts interestingly with the Pilgrimage, so there's some allure there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T15:52:24-08:00","id":11639,"title":"","content":"Mummy I'd say actually has the most crossover potential - You die and keep coming back? Me too! You're pursuing Apotheosis? I'm on a Pilgrimage to Humanity! You can cause droughts and natural disasters? I wish I could stop!<br /> <br /> The main issue would be the Arisen would look down on Prometheans as pale, broken imitations, And they wouldn't be wrong, really, as it sucks so much to be a Promethean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}